              <br>
        <p>Having used up all of our Gibson product for previous transformations and diagnostics, we assembled the pcrA-pUS212 construct again and reran our transformations, with <i>E. coli </i> DH5α in addition. This time, we saw growth after around 36 hours in the plates using <i>E. coli </i> Nissle cells. The growth seemed to be similar in the knockout and no knockout plates.</p>
