        <p>Unfortunately, after colony PCR and gel electrophoresis of the transformed cultures, we realized the Gibson assembly for this round had actually failed after sequencing results came back. Only the plasmid backbone was taken up, conferring chloramphenicol resistance without the pcrA insert.</p>
        <p>After reperforming Gibson assembly and transformation, the project was able to successfully liquid culture transformed Nissle cells (both Δlpp and without Δlpp). We sent out the transformed construct via sequencing and SDS-page of expressed proteins.</p>

