      <h3 class="h3">MKIV</h3>       
        <p>Building on the “backpack” motor module design concept, we began to wonder <span class="span">why not take it a step further and make the LED panels and heat pads modular as well?</span> Key interviews with an external advisor and an external advisor informed these changes. This shift later became the primary focus of our hardware development. In the MKIV design, we fully considered the needs of PRoSPER and synthetic biology applications for a bioreactor.</p>
        <p class="listtitle">We believe the bioreactor should have:</p>
          <ol>
            <li>Compact hardware footprint with large culture capacity.</li>
            <li>Given the remoteness of Mars mission, ARC should be able to serve as a versatile benchtop bioreactor for laboratory applications.</li>
            <li>Compatible with sterilization protocol.</li>
            <li>Rapid adaptability to new model organisms.</li>
